  "hunk_limits": [
    "Existing host helpers: native protected setup/auth/provision/recovery/owner/custody/release consumer only; no browser/gateway startup/capability, no selected task/adoption service imports. Preserve existing source behavior and accepted worker repairs.",
    "Host lib/service/listener/supervisor/instance/human: exact native composition, same-connection lifetimes/CH-LIFE revisions and locks; browser status must remain unavailable until real consumer. Preserve future consumers in original reservoirs.",
    "Native protocol/worker paths: dedicated public record and retained CH-LIFE completion/registry/event behavior only. No accepted HQ/admission/crypto semantics rewrite.",
    "Host release runtime: defer only unused private gateway_binding method; retain complete verification and runtime pinned image admission.",
    "Cargo.lock/org-host Cargo: add only retained pinned hmac/org-release/tar0.4.46/flate2 1.1.11/cc1.11.1/ring0.17.14 needed by actual imports, inspect exact generated lock delta; no unrelated upgrades.",
    "Host build.rs and opener_build_pins.rs: exact retained native ARC bridge bytes/SDK frameworks+bsm and build-pinned release trust embedding; preserve release debug refusal, strict token pin and independent source guards. No guard weakening or blanket b77 guard copy.",
    "apps/agentic-org/src/lib.rs: only native recovery command registration if real human transport available; do not enable fake successful setup or task commands.",
    "Tests: keep all meaningful native/custody/recovery/release/channel tests; preserve task/browser assertions with their actual later consumer in reservoirs and record exact deferral, no no-op or cfg-disabled production shim.",
    "Use accepted org_proto::work::{JournalPosition,WriterIdentity} paths for those retained pure canonical types; never import selected_tasks to satisfy old path references.",
    "Carry native fixtures and actual production calls without enabling unfinished browser/task semantics. All accepted F3b source repairs and tests remain. Startup and v3 integration test edits are only required channel/recovery caller hunks, never wholesale overwrite from older source.",
    "No worker/source guard/check policy edits beyond explicitly named reviewed opener_build_pins.rs native/build trust token-pin update. No commits/push/branchswitch/acceptance or metadata/catalog edits by delegate. Source grant candidate hashes bind preimplementation; root already owns declared checklist/task metadata."
  ],
